<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to sell K&amp;H bank to Belgium, Irish firms.</title>
<headline>Hungary to sell K&amp;H bank to Belgium, Irish firms.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's privatisation agency APV said on Wednesday that it would sell Kereskedelmi Bank (K&amp;H) to the consortium of Belgium's Kredietbank and Ireland's Irish Life Plc.</p>
<p>&quot;The consortium has put forward an unprecedentedly good offer,&quot; APV chairman Arpad Kovacs told a news conference.</p>
<p>He added that the consortium had offered $30 million, or 567.3 percent of the nominal value, for the one billion forint stake.</p>
</text>
